<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Player Etiquette</h1>
<p>Welcome to Valhalla! We hope you enjoy playing here. This page tells you 
what is expected of players, and what you can expect of the admins.
</p><p><b>New to muds?</b> Most people are, at first, and many panic. Don't worry, 
you are not alone; we have all been there.
</p><p><b>Don't shout for help.</b> Shouting "I am new and lost, what do I do?" 
the moment you arrive annoys players and admins alike; nobody likes 
people shouting left and right. Whining doesn't help either: not everyone 
will like everything about this mud, but complaining only drives other 
players away.
</p><p><b>How to get help:</b>
</p>
<ul><li>Take the automated newbie tour in Udgaard. Until you reach level 6, you can call the tour guide back by typing: say help me newbie guide</li>
<li>Ask on the newbie channel: comm add newbie, then newbie &lt;your question&gt; (see <a cmd='#'>Help Comm</a>). Players there are glad to help.</li>
<li><a cmd='#'>who</a> shows who is online; tell a player your question directly. Most players are happy to help someone who asks politely.</li>
<li>Only when that fails, ask an admin (see <a cmd='#'>Help Immortal</a>): the admins are here to keep the game running, and try to let the world run itself.</li></ul>
<p><b>In short:</b> politeness and respect. People respect you if you respect 
them. Be helpful and kind when you can. The admins are here for you, but 
not at your every whim: they are busy improving the game, and they are 
here to enjoy it too.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
